	(text "SSR DRIVE x2 - HIGH SIDE, GROUND-REFERENCED (rev B.4)\nEach terminal's + is switched by a 60 V P-channel LP2309LT1G (Q5/Q6)\noff SSR_24V; the - pin is board GND, so an SSR lead chafed onto the\nearthed enclosure is a non-event, not a bypass. The GPIO drives an opto\nLED, never a gate: at 24 V a gate-to-drain failure would put 240 mA\ninto the pin. The opto pulls the gate down through 10k (R69/R70); the\n8.2 V zener (D13/D14) sets V_SG from the rail, not from CTR, and R7/R20\nhold the gate at the source against the opto's dark current. D9/D10\nfreewheel a contactor coil; LED3/LED4 read the terminal itself.\nNOT an isolation barrier - see DESIGN-NOTES.md (SSR block)."
		(at 22 41.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "6304913f-3127-4b07-a0ad-875422d4f8c7")
	)
	(text "HARDWARE WATCHDOG\nU10 retriggerable one-shot: every rising edge on WDT_KICK restarts a\n~2.2 s window, so Q stays high only while firmware keeps kicking.\nQ holds Q3 on; Q3 pulls SSR_PG down, turning on high-side Q4, which\nsupplies SSR_EN (+5 V). SSR_EN enhances Q7, which pulls the gate of the\n24 V high-side switch Q9 down through R71 (D12 clamps V_SG to 8.2 V);\nQ9 feeds SSR_24V to both channels. Window expired: SSR_EN falls, R22\npulls Q9's gate to its source, SSR_24V is dead and both terminals are\noff whatever the channel switches are doing. R46/C38/C49 set the window.\nR48 holds B low when the MCU is high-Z. R47 is the fail-safe pull-up.\nSJ2 = bring-up defeat, REMOVE for service."
		(at 147.3333 38.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "cda228b3-5467-47fc-ac68-8d02f87ff9ec")
	)
